---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '');
---
<BaseLayout title="Your landscape dashboard">
  <section class="hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">ANDROID TABLET DASHBOARD · PUBLIC BETA</p>
    <h1>See what’s happening.<br />Keep the next action close.</h1>
    <p class="lead">Live quota, named chats and large touch controls beside your Mac. Inspired by the ESP32 Codex monitor, built for a landscape Android tablet.</p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button" href={`${base}/releases/`}>Download the beta</a>
      <a class="button secondary" href={`${base}/install/`}>Set up your tablet</a>
    </div>
    <figure>
      <img class="dashboard" src={`${base}/landscape-dashboard.png`} width="1280" height="800" alt="Landscape dashboard showing remaining quota, live chats, six Desktop agent slots, command keys and voice controls." />
      <figcaption>Flutter-rendered preview with sample data. Actual chats and lighting come from your connections.</figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>
  <section class="grid" aria-label="Dashboard features">
    <article class="card"><h2>See your workspace</h2><p>Five-hour and weekly quota remaining, reset countdowns, and named chats with running or attention states from your monitor bridge.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h2>Act from your desk</h2><p>Six Desktop Micro slots, command keys and directional controls. Hold to talk, Voice and Send stay within easy reach.</p></article>
    <article class="card"><h2>Choose your connection</h2><p>Bluetooth LE is the default. Rooted USB HID is available experimentally on the tested Lenovo Tab M8. Wi-Fi bridge status works independently.</p></article>
  </section>
  <section class="card"><h2>Voice uses your Mac microphone</h2><p>The tablet sends Micro gestures to the Mac. Its stock USB audio driver does not expose a usable tablet microphone. Select your preferred input on the Mac.</p><p><a href={`${base}/about/`}>Read capabilities and current limits →</a></p></section>
</BaseLayout>
